tools.description:
Close browser tabs by one selection mode: `tab_ids` (explicit), `match` (substring of title/URL), or `duplicates` (every tab sharing a URL with an earlier one). Set `dry_run` to preview the exact tabs that would close without touching them. Destructive — closed tabs cannot be recovered through this tool.

CRITICAL: You MUST explicitly ask the user for confirmation before running this tool with dry_run=false, unless they already asked you to.

Examples:
- {"tab_ids": [123, 456], "dry_run": true}
- {"match": "github.com", "dry_run": false}
- {"duplicates": true, "dry_run": true}

Returns:
  JSON object containing:
  - dry_run (boolean): Whether this was a preview
  - reason (string): Description of selection criteria
  - count/closed (int): Number of tabs matched/closed
  - by_domain (object): Map of domain to count
  - sample (array): First 10 tabs with {id, title}
